course: dictionary
lesson: 1882
title: Collective: one word, many people
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Collective means done or shared by all the members of a group together. «That is called collective punishment, and it is not fair to the others.» Here collective tells you the punishment falls on a whole group, not just one person.
explain: Collective can also be a noun: a group of people who work together and share what they make or own, like a farmers' collective. In grammar, a collective noun is a word for a group, like a team, a class, a herd or a flock of sheep.
explain: Check the meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «A collective noun names a group, like a team, a class, a herd or a flock of sheep.» Herd and flock both name groups of animals, so they are collective nouns.
fact: Collective means done or shared by all members of a group together.
fact: A collective noun names a group, like a team, a class, a herd or a flock of sheep.
fact: «Punishing a whole group for what one person did is called collective punishment; it is unfair to those who did nothing.»
fact: A collective can also be a group of people who work together and share what they make or own.
fact: Other collective nouns include a pride of lions and a swarm of bees.
exercise: Which word is a collective noun? | *herd | run | cat | happy
exercise: «Punishing a whole group for what one person did is called collective punishment.» What does collective mean here? | Very loud | Done by one person alone | *Shared by the whole group | Made of glass
exercise: A farmers' collective shares its tools and sells its crops together. What is a collective? | A type of tractor | A wild animal | *A group who work together and share | A single farmer working alone
test: In «a swarm of bees», which word is the collective noun? | of | a | *swarm | bees
test: «That is called collective punishment, and it is not fair to the others.» What is unfair about collective punishment? | It happens only at night | It rewards everyone | It is a kind of sport | *It punishes people who did nothing
exam: Which sentence shows collective effort? | It rained all afternoon | *The whole class cleaned the park together | Mia tidied her desk alone | The dog ran to the gate
